        "title": "Medieval Archaeology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMEDIEVAL VILLAGE FORMS:\n  NUCLEATED VILLAGES (common in England, N. France, N. Germany):\n    Clustered houses around a green, church, or manor\n    Open-field system: strips in communal fields; complex rotation\n    Deserted medieval villages (DMVs): entire village abandonment\n    → Causes: Black Death (1348–50); enclosure; bad harvests; landlord clearing\n    → UK: 3,000+ DMVs identified; many from aerial photography"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-MEDIEVAL-ARCHAEOLOGY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "07-MEDIEVAL-ARCHAEOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
