      },
      "text": "LONGHOUSE:\n  Standard vernacular house: humans and livestock under one roof\n    → Warmth from animals; shared entrance; byre at one end\n  Wall: timber, cruck frame, or stone foundation\n  Roof: thatch or turf; leaves minimal trace archaeologically\n  → Identified by: wall slot/post-holes, hearth, midden (refuse) deposit\n```"
    },
